      "writtenOn": "2025-01-21T19:36:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As much as possible we want to move away from any form of \"registration\" / \"global\" to set. This has run into huge issues with using Skia as a library as any global makes it more difficult for a library to use Skia (at the moment it is really only possible to use Skia from application code).\n\nIn other words, we really do just want an interface and then have an object of an implementation of that interface passed in from the user of Skia.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 17,
        "startChar": 17,
        "endLine": 17,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "e9a134203fd97f69f98af585a19db856f0f36bb5",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2f04c8c3_75e1c0bb",
        "filename": "include/pathops/SkPathOps.h",
        "patchSetId": 22
      },
      "lineNbr": 32,
      "author": {
        "id": 5140
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-21T19:36:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If we\u0027re going through all this work to rename everything, why not make pathops an interface? Even if for the first pass we just always create a new one (of a specific implementation type, with no state) and then call the method on it. In other words, why this rename which leaves everything static? SkPathOps is currently set up like the old SkFontHost and what we want is an interface more like SkFontMgr.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 32,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 32,
        "endChar": 23
      },
      "revId": "e9a134203fd97f69f98af585a19db856f0f36bb5",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b271e638_d24b5cbd",
        "filename": "src/pathops/SkPathOpsDispatch.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 22
      },
      "lineNbr": 21,
      "author": {
        "id": 5140
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-21T19:36:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "No, this needs to be avoided like the plague. No more global registration. Just pass the thing in like SkFontMgr is now.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 21,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 21,
        "endChar": 39
      },
      "revId": "e9a134203fd97f69f98af585a19db856f0f36bb5",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b8ee7056_9a1347c3",
        "filename": "src/pathops/SkPathOpsDispatch.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 22
      },
      "lineNbr": 21,
      "author": {
        "id": 5642
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-21T21:07:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "How would this work in practice?\n\nUnlike SkFontMgr, which reflects a core dependency for font-related functionality, PathOps use is pretty much an implementation detail which tends to pop up in random places.  Are you thinking of plumbing the interface through all the APIs (public and private) which happen to be currently terminating in these random spots?",
      "parentUuid": "b271e638_d24b5cbd",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 21,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 21,
        "endChar": 39
      },
      "revId": "e9a134203fd97f69f98af585a19db856f0f36bb5",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f463db72_126b2021",
        "filename": "src/pathops/SkPathOpsDispatch.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 22
      },
      "lineNbr": 21,
      "author": {
        "id": 5140
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-21T21:12:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, absolutely. Otherwise there is no point to any of this. Just compile in a different implementation otherwise.",
      "parentUuid": "b8ee7056_9a1347c3",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 21,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 21,
        "endChar": 39
      },
      "revId": "e9a134203fd97f69f98af585a19db856f0f36bb5",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "66555a50_1fab12d0",
        "filename": "src/pathops/SkPathOpsDispatch.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 22
      },
      "lineNbr": 21,
      "author": {
        "id": 5642
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-22T13:22:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That would make sense if we already had a `skia_lib_ctx` being passed around consistently.  So let\u0027s do that first, instead of polluting unrelated public APIs with pathops gunk (which again is mostly an implementation detail for random bits of skia) and introducing significant client code refactors for a feature that afaik nobody is asking for.\n\nThe approach here should not preclude further runtime decoupling when we have a sane framework in place.",
      "parentUuid": "f463db72_126b2021",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 21,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 21,
        "endChar": 39
      },
      "revId": "e9a134203fd97f69f98af585a19db856f0f36bb5",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c6525277_6c35ae32",
        "filename": "src/pathops/SkPathOpsDispatch.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 22
      },
      "lineNbr": 21,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-29T15:24:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "After talking offline with Mike, I am not opposed to temporarily having global registration for something that is a fairly isolated component, particularly if there is follow up work to further remove dependencies from within Skia to pathops. This change is a step towards that decoupling, but it would be nice if this comment can suggest that direction and emphasize that runtime registration is not necessarily the end goal (e.g. perhaps we\u0027ll have a raster context object at some point, or we won\u0027t need pathops in core).",
      "parentUuid": "66555a50_1fab12d0",
      "range": {
